' 4+1 process view - Player cancels (US19) · the window read at that moment, and two cancellations at the same time
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes code and whoever debugs.
' Documented decision: The cancellation window read at that moment, and the lock that turns two simultaneous cancellations into one (US19).
' Not drawn: internal detail of the classes; refusals that do not change the sequence (they are in the text of process.md).
@startuml process-cancel-player
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - player cancels (US19): the window read at that moment, and two cancellations at the same time
autonumber

participant "My bookings" as WEB_F_MYBOOK
box "ASP.NET Core API"
  participant "Cancel" as API_BOOK_MINE
  participant "Pitch lock" as CC_LOCK
  participant "Put in the outbox" as API_NOTIF_OUTBOX
end box
database "PostgreSQL" as C_DB

WEB_F_MYBOOK -> API_BOOK_MINE : POST /api/bookings/{id}/cancel [apiJson; Player policy]
API_BOOK_MINE -> C_DB : the booking's pitch_id, only if it belongs to the session's player (404\nbooking_not_found) [SELECT bookings]
group Lock transaction
  API_BOOK_MINE -> CC_LOCK : LockAsync(pitchId)
  CC_LOCK -> C_DB : BEGIN; SELECT 1 FROM pitches … FOR UPDATE [SQL]
  API_BOOK_MINE -> C_DB : Reads the booking again (with tracking) [SELECT bookings]
  API_BOOK_MINE -> C_DB : The club's window now, never the booking's [SELECT\nclubs.cancellation_window_hours]
  API_BOOK_MINE -> API_BOOK_MINE : booking.CancelByPlayer(window, now) → CancellationOutcome
  alt NotConfirmed
    API_BOOK_MINE --> WEB_F_MYBOOK : 422 booking_not_confirmed (ROLLBACK on dispose)
  else OutsideWindow (now ≥ startsAt − window)
    API_BOOK_MINE --> WEB_F_MYBOOK : 422 outside_cancellation_window, extension cancellationDeadline\n(UTC)
  else Cancelled
    API_BOOK_MINE -> API_NOTIF_OUTBOX : EnqueuePlayerCancellationAsync(booking)
    API_BOOK_MINE -> C_DB : SaveChanges: UPDATE bookings (CancelledByPlayer, cancelled_at) and\nINSERT outbox_messages [SQL]
    CC_LOCK -> C_DB : COMMIT; the slot is free again (the constraint only sees\nConfirmed) [SQL]
    API_BOOK_MINE --> WEB_F_MYBOOK : 200 MyBookingResponse
  end
end

== Two cancellations of the same booking at the same time (two tabs, double click) ==

WEB_F_MYBOOK -> API_BOOK_MINE : Request A: POST …/cancel
WEB_F_MYBOOK -> API_BOOK_MINE : Request B: POST …/cancel
CC_LOCK -> C_DB : A gets FOR UPDATE; B waits on the same pitches row\n[SQL]
API_BOOK_MINE -> C_DB : A: reads Confirmed again, cancels, COMMIT [SQL]
API_BOOK_MINE -> C_DB : B: gets the lock and reads the booking, already CancelledByPlayer [SQL]
API_BOOK_MINE --> WEB_F_MYBOOK : A: 200
API_BOOK_MINE --> WEB_F_MYBOOK : B: 422 booking_not_confirmed (never 500, never two emails)
@enduml
